schema:description:
This system manages the digital versions of legal agreements, benefit packages, and standardized price lists (tariffs). It provides a central repository for the rules and prices that govern the financial relationship between payers and providers.&#xD;
&#xD;
Its purpose is to ensure that all participants in the health network work with the same up-to-date information for billing and payments. It reduces disputes and administrative errors by providing a transparent and auditable source for contract terms and prices.&#xD;
&#xD;
Example: A version-controlled system that ensures a hospital is paid the 2026 standardized rate for a cardiac procedure.
